PLUM ecoNET Cloud for Home Assistant

This community project was developed for a Home Assistant user installation
with assistance from OpenAI Codex. It is not an official PLUM, SPIROFLEX or
Home Assistant project.

Protocol references:
- The ecoNET Cloud web application, https://econetcloud.eu/.
- m-szopinski/econet-api-client,
  https://github.com/m-szopinski/econet-api-client.
  Version 1.0.7 declares the ISC license in its package metadata. It was used
  as a protocol/signature reference; its TypeScript implementation is not
  bundled in this repository.
- AWS Cognito, Signature Version 4 and MQTT protocol specifications.

Runtime dependency:
- pycognito 2024.5.1 (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/pvizeli/pycognito.
  It and its dependencies are installed through Home Assistant's dependency
  management, not vendored here. Their licenses remain applicable.

The small profile fixture in tests contains hand-assembled interface facts
(parameter identifiers and supported options), not a complete manufacturer
profile, firmware, web application or manufacturer graphics. The icon in
custom_components/econet_cloud/brand/ was drawn for this project.

The optional PV examples are adaptations of the project's own Home Assistant
automations, using generic placeholder entities. ecoNET300 itself is a
separate project maintained at
https://github.com/jontofront/ecoNET-300-Home-Assistant-Integration
and derived from pblxptr's original implementation; its code is not bundled.
